Removes draft 54's serve-mismatch observation from the simulated host
(be31269): a source that finds a candidate out of step with its record
while serving tells its engine nothing, as before. A chmod its watcher
missed is refused but never observed, and if its user undoes it before a
scan, nothing is ever announced and the peer it refused is never told to
ask again (DESIGN.md §7.5 step 2). Seed 4013 (--nodes 2 --steps 200)
showed it on main from 841fe16 on; since drafts 52 and 53's failed-report
rules its history no longer reaches it, and no seed does in 44,300 run
with this patch (0 to 1,999 and the 76,000, 86,000 and 96,000 slices at
the defaults, and 0 to 19,999 in two-node and in three-node worlds at 200
steps), so the fix's unit test stands in for a pinned seed.

